{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS83V6kKEXi7TstdB7Lx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Connect flow is fixed in the code, and I tested it end to end against a local stub. I have not tested it against real Intervals.icu. The causes are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Causes**\n1. **The button can't authenticate.** It was a plain `<a href>` GET, and a page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization` header. Every click got a 401. Init is now a POST that returns `authorize_url` as JSON, and the SPA navigates to it.\n2. **The scope string repeated areas.** `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR` were each listed twice, and Intervals rejected the authorize request. The calendar scopes are the recent change that broke the pasted-link workaround too. The scope is now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`.\n3. **The one-hour reconnect was our assumption.** With no `expires_in` in the response, the server defaulted to 3600 seconds. Intervals tokens don't expire, so Rivera's connection was marked expired while still valid. I removed the expiry and the refresher. A 401 from Intervals now clears the token and shows \"expired, reconnect\".\n\n**Colleague's note**\n- Applied: no refresh token and handle revocation on a 401; each scope area once; POST init returning JSON.\n- Not applied: encrypting tokens at rest (that belongs with the prod Postgres table), dropping `grant_type` and `redirect_uri` (our log shows the exchange succeeded with them), the JWT state with a `purpose` claim, and the account-mismatch guard. None of these caused the reported failures.\n\n**Not verified**\n- The live Intervals flow. I tested against a local stub, which accepts the new scope, rejects the old one with `Duplicate scope`, and covers revocation. Our logs only show `invalid_request`, so the duplicate scope is the likely cause, not a confirmed one.\n- The redirect URI `http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/callback` needs to be registered on the Intervals OAuth client.\n- A `server.py` started before my edits (PID 94527) is still running on port 8766 with the old code. I left it alone since it isn't mine. Restart it before testing.\n\nI didn't commit anything. The changes are in `config.py`, `server.py`, `static/app.js`, and the new `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3493,"cache_read_input_tokens":55245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3493},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aba06b00-3971-45c3-ac2c-cacd306a797b","uuid":"ddf95b97-b359-4834-b7c7-0e3aa14c08b0","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:37:09.770Z","request_id":"req_011CgS83UpscP7jPheeQCPBY"}
